\fs36 \cf2 Research Abstract: Mapping the Stability Portfolio\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 This study utilizes a high-fidelity analytical pipeline to examine the "Stability Gap" across disparate economic geographies in the United States, categorized as the 
\f0\b "Three Countries"
\f1\b0  (Bottom, Middle, and Top income terciles). By analyzing the 2023 IPUMS CPS Annual Social and Economic (ASEC) microdata, this research establishes 
\f0\b Weighted Population Prevalence Rates
\f1\b0  for key economic security anchors. Anchored on a population universe of 
\f0\b 146,133 person-records
\f1\b0 , the analysis incorporates all individuals\'97regardless of labor force participation\'97to create a statistically accurate national denominator for Americans aged 
\f0\b 25 and older
\f1\b0 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

